{"id": "EUVD-2026-93335", "enisaUuid": "3f104a9f-be56-3c4b-b262-641c161cd282", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: brcmfmac: cyw: pass PMKID to firmware if present\n\nZero out auth_status on initialization. Otherwise, garbage will\nleak from the stack to the firmware (when ssid is less than 32 bytes\nand/or when params->pmkid is set). Then, pass the params->pmkid to the\nfirmware (without it, the firmware caches a garbage PMKID on successful\nauthentication and denies a subsequent association request that includes\nthe PMKID).", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:18:01", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c2cf589c7d546557ed60c43f2ec014279265dfbf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6fba6233e9ca7718661e53555a3961c58772c21a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e2de8d5eb2984416affdd9559e55f37c7f1bbf47"], "aliases": ["GHSA-c6xm-v6x8-64wh", "CVE-2026-98350"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a5801b0-2c10-3576-9104-4be78147bef7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.16"}, {"id": "402ad212-3dff-3281-94ef-3784fcc99ff7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "66f909308a7c05082919ff214a0bbe2a76aa0283 <6fba6233e9ca7718661e53555a3961c58772c21a"}, {"id": "729f0028-b2ff-35bd-9940-ad869dd39319", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "affeb1de-6ba0-346c-a665-dccaaaf0f148", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "b6e990ae-6525-3998-bae8-fd5204913f49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "e4548640-a9e4-3bfb-b932-b16df4665f98", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "66f909308a7c05082919ff214a0bbe2a76aa0283 <c2cf589c7d546557ed60c43